<<<
D:—The people are now returning & trying to again get together a home./With us outside the Treaty, we must expect the Commission to at least neglect our interests.
===
D:—*The people are now returning & trying* to again get together *a home./With us outside the Treaty, we must expect the Commission* to at least neglect *our interests.*
>>>

<<<
it is easy to write to get a home together again, &, as again does not belong to the single word get, but to get a home together, nothing is gained
===
it is easy to write *to get a home together again*, &, as *again* does not belong to the single word *get*, but to *get a home together*, nothing is gained
>>>

<<<
In the second, at least cannot be put before to because it would then go with Commission (=the Commission, even if not other people), nor after neglect because it would then be doubtful whether it referred back to neglect or forward to interests, nor after interests because it would then belong either to interests or to neglect our interests
===
In the second, *at least* cannot be put before *to* because it would then go with *Commission* (=the Commission, even if not other people), nor after *neglect* because it would then be doubtful whether it referred back to *neglect* or forward to *interests*, nor after *interests* because it would then belong either to *interests* or to *neglect our interests*
>>>

<<<
it - secures our realizing that the writer has in mind some other verb such as injure or oppose with which the weaker neglect is to be contrasted.
===
it secures our realizing that the writer has in mind some other verb such as *injure* or *oppose* with which the weaker *neglect* is to be contrasted.
>>>

<<<
we have not so much a misplacing of _ the adverb as a violence done to the verb.
===
we have not so much a misplacing of the adverb as a violence done to the verb.
>>>

